@startuml OPS-Session-Utilization-Workflow
title Session Workflow - Add Timetable Sessions and Log Faculty Utilization
hide empty description

start
:Coordinator+ requests to add a session\nor log actual utilization;
if (Authenticated, authorized and batch in caller's scope?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Reject with authorization or scope error;
  stop
endif
if (Batch is Completed?) then (yes)
  :Reject session changes;
  stop
endif

if (Add a planned timetable session?) then (yes)
  :Validate batch and session date within batch bounds;
  :Validate required topic and any supplied fields;
  if (Matching batch/date/module already exists?) then (yes)
    :Reject duplicate schedule row;
    stop
  else (no)
    :Infer day_name when omitted;
    :Create TrainingSession with status Scheduled;
    :Compute sequence number and week at read time;
    if (Faculty email available?) then (yes)
      :Send session-scheduled email;
    else (no)
      :Log faculty name without sending email;
    endif
  endif
endif

if (Import a timetable instead?) then (yes)
  :Upload supported Excel/CSV file;\nparse Flat, TOC, Curriculum or Topic-column format;
  :Preview extracted rows and validation errors;\nno persistence during ingest;
  if (Coordinator applies valid preview?) then (yes)
    :Revalidate batch scope, dates, duplicates,\nfaculty requirement and session count;
    if (Any row invalid or resulting count > training_days?) then (yes)
      :Reject entire apply; persist nothing;
      stop
    endif
    if (Missing session slots?) then (yes)
      if (Batch has default faculty and enough weekdays?) then (yes)
        :Add generated placeholder sessions;
      else (no)
        :Reject entire apply; persist nothing;
        stop
      endif
    endif
    :Persist all timetable rows atomically;\nset Scheduled and update schedule_complete;
  else (no)
    :Discard preview without persistence;
  endif
endif

if (Log actual delivery?) then (yes)
  :Validate batch scope, date bounds,\nvalid time window and required topic;
  :Resolve faculty by active user ID/name;\ntry Faculty-role matches, then active users;\nretain provided unmatched name as free text;
  if (No faculty name provided?) then (yes)
    :Reject with validation error;
    stop
  endif
  :Optionally link to TrainingSession timetable row;
  :Create FacultyUtilization record;\nstatus starts Scheduled;
  if (Status is Cancelled or Not Conducted?) then (yes)
    if (Outcome reason provided?) then (yes)
      :Set outcome actor and timestamp if omitted;
    else (no)
      :Reject; reason is required;
      stop
    endif
  endif
  :Recalculate batch average feedback\nwhen a rated completed delivery exists;
endif

while (Utilization is not terminal?) is (yes)
  if (Delivery underway?) then (yes)
    :Set status InProgress;
  endif

  if (Update utilization?) then (yes)
    :Validate scope, time window and batch date bounds;
    if (Attempt to set Completed through generic update?) then (yes)
      :Reject; Completed is reserved for Gate 1;
    else (no)
      :Apply allowed changes;
    endif
  endif

  if (Reschedule?) then (yes)
    :Require new date/time and valid time window;
    :Update date/time; reset status to Scheduled;\nrecord outcome reason, actor and timestamp;
  endif

  if (Cancel or mark Not Conducted?) then (yes)
    :Require outcome reason (minimum 3 characters);
    :Set terminal status, actor and timestamp;
    if (Linked timetable row exists?) then (yes)
      :Synchronize timetable status;
    endif
  endif

  if (Complete delivery through Gate 1?) then (yes)
    if (Already Completed, Cancelled or Not Conducted?) then (yes)
      :Reject with 409 Conflict;
    else (no)
      :Validate rating 1.0-5.0,\ntopic feedback >= 3 characters,\nstudents present >= 0;
      if (Feedback valid?) then (yes)
        :Set status Completed and feedback_submitted;
        :Store rating and feedback notes;
        :Mark linked timetable row Completed;
        :Recalculate batch_avg_feedback\nfrom rated Completed deliveries only;
      else (no)
        :Return validation error;
      endif
    endif
  endif
endwhile (no)

:Session outcome is terminal:\nCompleted, Cancelled or Not Conducted;
:Batch closure remains separate and requires\nall sessions terminal plus a rated delivery;
stop

note right
Faculty time-overlap/double-booking across batches
is not checked during schedule import or delivery logging.

TrainingSession is the planned timetable; FacultyUtilization
is the actual delivery ledger. A utilization may optionally
link to a timetable row.
end note
@enduml
